"}, "word": "kvittera"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive, figurative) To bring to a common level or plane, in respect of rank, condition, character, privilege, etc.", "tags": ["figuratively", "transitive"], "examples": ["to level all the ranks and conditions of men"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "võrtsustama"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "rihitama"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "ühtlustama"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "tasoittaa"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive) To adjust or adapt to a certain level.", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": ["to level remarks to the capacity of children"], "quotes": [{"text": "For all his mind on honour fixed is, / To which he levels all his purposes.", "reference": "1591, Ed[mund] Sp[enser], “Prosopopoia. Or Mother Hubberds Tale.”, in Complaints. Containing Sundrie Small Poemes of the Worlds Vanitie. […], London: […] William Ponsonbie, […], →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "нивелирам"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "sovittaa jonkun tason mukaiseksi"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "tasata"}, {"language": {"code": "bo", "name": "Tibetan"}, "word": "སྙོམ"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive) To speak honestly and openly [with with ‘someone’] (see: level with).", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Sean, I'll level with you. This could get ugly. Do you have a gun?", "reference": "2010, James William Jones, Triple Crossed:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/level", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons